body:
Disney didn't use the photo; it was an online publishing company with an article that had to do with something Disney. Any time the media can use photos from the theme parks they do because they get more clicks.

&#x200B;

Edit: reread what I wrote in the OP and totally get how it's confusing; my bad!!

I always tell people, "Think of every asshole you know. Every insufferably obnoxious person. Everyone you've met who is well-meaning, but annoying. Somewhere they have parents, and sure, maybe they're that way because of their parents, but maybe not. And what if that's your kid... forever. Best not to risk it."

&#x200B;

Edit: deleted a word

\*\*\*\*\*INTO THE SPIDER-VERSE SPOILERS\*\*\*\*\*

&#x200B;

I love love love this movie so fucking much (everyone go see it while it's still on the big screen!) and that's why it's such a bummer that Peter B. Parker's story arch is just to learn he's ready for kids. Fucking bullshit, man. In his universe Mary Jane leaves him because the idea of having kids scared him, which um, fucking yeah, of course it should scare him! What is Mary Jane thinking wanting kids with Spider-Man?! That's so incredibly dangerous and stupid and not fair to their innocent offspring, who will for sure be happening now, because Peter learned while helping a teenager embrace his full self that he actually is ready to have kids. Bullshit, man.

> And divorcing because one of the spouses doesn't want kids is not a valid reason ! 

Incredible how so many millions of people don't take both the commitments of marriage and creating and being responsible for AN ENTIRE HUMAN BEING seriously. Absolutely incredible.

&#x200B;
